# Build output
/target/

# Crash and timeout artifacts generated by libfuzzer
/artifacts/

# WHY Cargo.lock IS tracked here, unlike cargo-fuzz's template default: this manifest resolves
# independently of the workspace lock, so leaving it ignored made `cargo check --manifest-path
# fuzz/Cargo.toml` re-resolve against live crates.io on every CI run. That check is REQUIRED, so an
# upstream publish could turn every open PR red with no repo change — which is exactly what happened:
# a fresh resolve dropped the feature unification that supplies zune-jpeg's `log` feature, its `warn!`
# collapsed to a no-op macro, and "macro expansion ends with an incomplete expression" blocked seven
# PRs at once while `main` stayed green because the job is PR-only.
# A required check must be reproducible; a binary crate's lock is tracked for precisely this reason.

# Coverage data
/coverage/
*.profraw
*.profdata

# WHY: libFuzzer generates hash-named corpus entries during runs.
# Seed files (corpus/*/seed_*) are hand-crafted and tracked in git.
# Generated entries match [0-9a-f]{40} — this pattern catches them.
/corpus/*/[0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f]*
